    exerciseHeading: "Plan an import with unresolved ownership",
    exercise: ["A fictional client wants a new system ready for its next reporting cycle. The data export contains inconsistent account identifiers. Sales has discussed a launch date, but the client has not named a data owner and the acceptance criteria are missing. You can coordinate the project but cannot change the contract.", "Prepare a kickoff agenda that exposes the dependency on clean identifiers. Identify what can proceed while the client confirms ownership. Ask who approves the imported result and what they will compare it with. Do not promise that a data cleanup tool can infer all correct matches."],
    tableCaption: "Kickoff agenda worksheet", columns: ["Agenda item", "Agreement to obtain"], rows: [["Outcome", "Which reporting workflow must work at launch?"],["Scope", "Which data and features are included or excluded?"],["Ownership", "Who resolves identifier problems and signs off the result?"],["Readiness", "What sample data proves the import can be tested?"],["Acceptance", "Which checks determine whether the delivered workflow is ready?"]],
